msgid "Add"
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding a disk to a degraded array starts the rebuild process. The kernel automatically syncs the data onto the new disk, which can take a very long time, so do not power off or reboot the system while it is in progress. Alternatively, a disk can be added to a healthy array as a <em>hot spare</em> that will be used automatically to replace a failed disk."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding disk(s) to the array reshapes it, which can take a very long time depending on its size. Do not power off or reboot the system while the reshape is in progress. Note that the file system on the array is not grown automatically."
msgstr ""

